"kind":"trace",
"id":"lateness_short",
"source":"lateness_short.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    tok = raw.split()\n    n = len(tok) // 2\n    jobs = []\n    pos = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        t = int(tok[pos])\n        d = int(tok[pos + 1])\n        pos += 2\n        jobs.append((d, t))\n\n    jobs.sort()\n\n    clock = 0\n    peak = -10 ** 9\n    for d, t in jobs:\n        clock += t\n        late = clock - d\n        peak = max(peak, late)\n\n    print(peak)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The program reads time and deadline pairs, sorts the jobs by deadline, then runs them one after another, computing each job's lateness as its finish time minus its deadline and keeping the largest one in peak.",
"presets":[
